Z||000000||Jefrysuko||07-15-2001||12:08 PM||||Last friday as I walked into work a coworker told me he had something to look at.  He had a automobile trade magazine in his hand and pointed this out to me.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86_SE_add.jpg"> <BR>That night I took the wife and her Thunderbird to the dealership to look at the car.  We had been wanting to get rid of the T-bird since it had been backed into by a Ryder truck and we noticed that the floor pans were rusting.  Upon arival we saw that the fiero had a typical stuck headlight and a few other things that were going to help with negotiations.  The batery was dead and salesman didn't know why.  Upon getting a jump and figuring out how to start the car (tricky alarm), I decided to see if I could get the headlight down.  I turned the nob and the headlight spun right down but kept spinning.  Turn the headlights on and it goes up but keeps spinning again.  This is when the porter tells me that is the reason that the battery was dead.  So I take the salesman over to the T-bird where he gives me some jive on what the car is worth and when I am about to walk away he offers me a "even trade."  So I take the Fiero for a spin and it drives fairly nice.  We go back and fill out the paperwork and now I have Fiero number two.  I disconected the headlight motor for the ride home and the porter looks at me and says "you know how to fix that?"  To which I say "of course" with a big smile.<P>So what do you guy's think?  Did I do good?<P>------------------<BR>Jeffrey D Suckow<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:Jefrysuko@aol.com">Jefrysuko@aol.com</A>      <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Zippy_11_sig.jpg">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT_4.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||jake1852||07-15-2001||12:12 PM||||congrats, man. you kicked ass.<P>------------------<BR>- Unfinished ferrari kit, custom made myself<BR>-87 duke (just got it, its fast, and i dont know why yet!)<BR>- 87 GT<BR>- Tc Maserati (daily drive)||||reg||1
